    <div style="background:#1e293b;padding:20px;border-radius:12px;margin-bottom:20px;border:1px solid #334155;">
    <h3 style="color:#7dd3fc;margin-top:0;">📖 Glossary</h3>
    <div style="overflow-x:auto;margin:12px 0;">
    <table style="width:100%;border-collapse:collapse;color:#f1f5f9;">
    <tr style="background:#334155;">
    <th style="padding:10px;border:1px solid #475569;text-align:left;">Term</th>
    <th style="padding:10px;border:1px solid #475569;text-align:left;">Meaning</th>
    </tr>
    <tr>
    <td style="padding:10px;border:1px solid #475569;vertical-align:top;"><strong style="color:#fde68a;">Similar</strong>
    </td>
    <td style="padding:10px;border:1px solid #475569;vertical-align:top;">Same shape; equal angles and proportional sides.</td>
    </tr>
    <tr style="background:#172033;">
    <td style="padding:10px;border:1px solid #475569;vertical-align:top;"><strong style="color:#fde68a;">Enlargement</strong>
    </td>
    <td style="padding:10px;border:1px solid #475569;vertical-align:top;">Transformation with a centre and scale factor.</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
    <td style="padding:10px;border:1px solid #475569;vertical-align:top;"><strong style="color:#fde68a;">Linear scale factor</strong>
    </td>
    <td style="padding:10px;border:1px solid #475569;vertical-align:top;">Ratio of image length to object length.</td>
    </tr>
    <tr style="background:#172033;">
    <td style="padding:10px;border:1px solid #475569;vertical-align:top;"><strong style="color:#fde68a;">Centre of enlargement</strong>
    </td>
    <td style="padding:10px;border:1px solid #475569;vertical-align:top;">The fixed point of an enlargement.</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
    <td style="padding:10px;border:1px solid #475569;vertical-align:top;"><strong style="color:#fde68a;">Invariant point</strong>
    </td>
    <td style="padding:10px;border:1px solid #475569;vertical-align:top;">A point that does not move under a transformation.</td>
    </tr>
    </table>
    </div>
    </div>
